# DURABLE REPRO — `.unwrap_or_else()` with a RESOURCE payload makes the
# COMPILER PANIC. Third failure mode of the Option/Result combinator family.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD):
#   `gg check` -> "OK: no semantic errors"
#   `gg build` -> PANIC:
#       Tier 2a consume-site violation: 1 violation(s) in module '<unknown>'.
#       First: fn @main bb2 i2 — AssignIntoOwnedSlot(dst: Money)
#              — untracked source consumed (ownership not decided).
#       at src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:2127
#
# So the accept/reject surface says yes and the build then dies. A user cannot
# tell from `gg check` that this program is unbuildable.
#
# ⚠ Worth reading carefully: the unconditional consume-site validator CAUGHT a
# real ownership hole here — the combinator lowering never decided ownership
# for the resource payload. That half is the system working. The defect is that
# it surfaces as a PANIC instead of a diagnostic, and that `gg check` does not
# see what the lowering validator does.
#
# ⚠ RESOURCE-PAYLOAD-SPECIFIC — the same shape over an `int` payload builds and
# runs fine, so a trivial-payload fixture is a false negative for this family.
#
# INTENDED: this program is well-typed and should build and print 11. (If the
# language instead decides the shape is illegal, the reference-grade answer is a
# `gg check` REJECTION with a diagnostic — never an accepted program that panics
# the compiler.) Either way today's behaviour is a defect.
#
# ORACLE: ggdef is OUT OF SUBSET for the combinator family (Core #9 note).
#
# Sibling costumes, same family, same round: `.map()`/`.filter()`/`.or_else()`
# silently empty the receiver; `.and_then()`/`.flat_map()` type-confuse into a
# SIGSEGV on C while LLVM refuses to compile the emitted IR. Full census in
# TODO.md — 6 of 7 combinators, 3 failure modes, all accepted by `gg check`.

struct Money:
    Vector[int] cents

struct Holder:
    Option[Money] slot

int size_of(Money m):
    return m.cents.len()

Vector[int] heap_cents(int n):
    Vector[int] c = Vector[int]()
    int i = 0
    while i < n:
        c.push(i)
        i = i + 1
    return c

Option[Money] make_opt(int n):
    return Some(Money(heap_cents(n)))

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(make_opt(11))
    Money r = h.slot.unwrap_or_else((): Money(heap_cents(9)))
    if h.slot is Some(m2):
        print(size_of(m2))
